import SiteLayout from '../components/SiteLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — Songdance"
  description="How SONGDANCE BV collects, uses, and protects your personal data — in plain language."
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="Legal"
    title="Privacy Policy"
    lede="What we collect, why, on what legal basis, how long we keep it, and what your rights are."
  />

  <section class="sd-section sd-prose sd-legal">
    <div class="sd-prose-inner">
      <p class="sd-legal-updated">Last update: 8 October 2026</p>

      <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
      <div class="sd-legal-block">
        <p><strong>SONGDANCE BV</strong></p>
        <p>Registered office: Beaupréstraat 13, 8310 Brugge, Belgium</p>
        <p>VAT: BE 0743.575.076</p>
        <p>Email: <a href="mailto:info@songdance.co">info@songdance.co</a></p>
        <p>Website: <a href="https://www.songdance.co">www.songdance.co</a></p>
      </div>
      <p>Songdance is the controller of the personal data described in this policy. We don’t have a data protection officer; for anything related to your data, write to <a href="mailto:info@songdance.co">info@songdance.co</a>.</p>

      <h2>2. What this policy covers</h2>
      <p>This policy applies to the Songdance website, the Songdance app (on the web, and for iPhone and Android), our online courses and memberships, live workshops and retreats, private sessions, our newsletter, and our certification program. It explains what we collect, why, on what legal basis, how long we keep it, and what your rights are.</p>
      <p>We try to say this in plain language. Where the law requires precise terms, we use them.</p>

      <h2>3. What we collect, and why</h2>
      <h3>3.1 When you buy or register</h3>
      <p>Name, email address, billing address, country, VAT number (for businesses), the product or program purchased, and payment status. Payment card details are handled entirely by our payment providers — we never see or store them.</p>
      <p><strong>Why:</strong> to perform the contract with you (Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR) and to meet bookkeeping and tax obligations (Art. 6(1)(c)).</p>
      <h3>3.2 When you join the newsletter or download a free resource</h3>
      <p>Email address, first name if you give it, and which resource you requested. We also record which emails you open and click, so we can stop sending things you ignore.</p>
      <p><strong>Why:</strong> your consent (Art. 6(1)(a)). You can withdraw it any time via the unsubscribe link in every email. If you’re an existing customer, we may send you information about similar programs on the basis of legitimate interest (Art. 6(1)(f)); the same unsubscribe link applies.</p>
      <h3>3.3 When you take part in courses and communities</h3>
      <p>Your profile in the Songdance app (and, until the circle has moved over to the app, on Mighty Networks), posts and comments you choose to make, the live sessions you say you will attend, and your progress through course materials. Section 3.8 describes the app in detail.</p>
      <p><strong>Why:</strong> to perform the contract (Art. 6(1)(b)) and our legitimate interest in running a functioning learning community (Art. 6(1)(f)).</p>
      <h3>3.4 Recordings of live online sessions</h3>
      <p>Live online sessions (Q&amp;As, group calls, online workshops) are recorded so participants can watch replays. The recording captures audio, video and chat of those who participate visibly.</p>
      <p><strong>Why:</strong> legitimate interest in making sessions available to participants who couldn’t attend live (Art. 6(1)(f)). You are told at the start of each session that recording is on. You can keep your camera off, mute yourself, rename yourself, or participate by chat only. If we want to use a recognizable clip of you for anything promotional, we will ask you separately first.</p>
      <h3>3.5 Retreat and program intake</h3>
      <p>For retreats and some in-depth programs we ask intake questions before confirming your place. Your answers may include information about your emotional and physical wellbeing, current life circumstances, and previous experience with this kind of work. Some of this is <strong>health-related data</strong>, which the GDPR treats as a special category.</p>
      <p><strong>Why:</strong> to assess together whether the program is right for you at this moment, and to allow the facilitators to hold the group well. The legal basis is your <strong>explicit consent</strong> (Art. 9(2)(a)), which you give when submitting the intake form. You can withhold or withdraw it — though without an intake we may not be able to confirm your participation in certain programs.</p>
      <p>Intake answers are read only by the facilitators of that program. They are never shared with other participants and never used for marketing. They are deleted within twelve months after the program ends, unless you ask us to keep them for a future program.</p>
      <h3>3.6 AI-assisted processing</h3>
      <p>We sometimes use AI tools (Anthropic’s Claude) to help summarize session transcripts and to help prepare intake assessments for the facilitators’ review. The AI output is a working document for the facilitator — <strong>decisions about participation are always made by a person, never by the system.</strong> Data sent to these tools is processed under a data processing agreement and is not used by the provider to train its models.</p>
      <p><strong>Why:</strong> legitimate interest in preparing sessions and intakes carefully and efficiently (Art. 6(1)(f)); for intake data, this happens within the scope of the explicit consent described in 3.5. If you’d rather your intake not be processed this way, say so in the form and a facilitator will read it directly instead.</p>
      <h3>3.7 When you visit the website</h3>
      <p>Standard technical data (IP address, browser, pages visited) and cookies. Strictly necessary cookies run on legitimate interest; analytics and any marketing cookies run only with your consent via the cookie banner. See the cookie notice on the site for the current list.</p>
      <h3>3.8 When you use the Songdance app</h3>
      <p><strong>Your account.</strong> Your email address, and any other email address you link because you bought with it; your name and, if you add them, a profile picture, an introduction and links; your language, the languages you read and your time zone; and when you confirmed that you are 18 or older and accepted the <a href="/community-guidelines">community guidelines</a>, the terms and this policy. If you sign in with Apple or Google, we receive your name, your email address (with Apple, possibly a private relay address) and an account identifier from them.</p>
      <p><strong>What you have access to.</strong> The app looks up your purchases on songdance.co by email address and records which courses, live sessions and passes you hold, from when and until when. Payment details never reach the app.</p>
      <p><strong>Signing in and security.</strong> Sign-in codes and sign-in links (stored only in scrambled form), one record per signed-in device (platform, device name, when it was last used), a short-lived counter per network address to stop abuse (the address itself is scrambled with a secret key and not stored), a log of changes to accounts and access, and server logs our host keeps for a few days.</p>
      <p><strong>Learning.</strong> Where you stopped in each class, which classes you marked as done, and the steps of your welcome checklist. Manuals you download stay on your phone; we do not see them there.</p>
      <p><strong>The circle.</strong> The posts, comments, hearts, answers, pictures, sound recordings and files you share, the spaces you belong to, and the reports and blocks you make. What you post is visible to the members of the space you post in. Hosts can remove posts and comments in their spaces.</p>
      <p><strong>Live sessions.</strong> The sessions you say you will attend, and, if you ask for one, a personal calendar address that lists them. Meetings are created on the host’s own Zoom account; your sign-up stays with us. When you join a call, Zoom’s own privacy policy applies to the call (see also 3.4 on recordings).</p>
      <p><strong>Practice together.</strong> The WhatsApp number you choose to enter, with the moment you agreed to its use; your availability, bookings and requests; and whether a session took place. Your number is shown only to a partner whose request you accepted, on that session’s page, and is hidden again once you have both confirmed or a day after the session. You can clear it at any time. The conversation itself happens in WhatsApp, under WhatsApp’s own terms.</p>
      <p><strong>Notifications.</strong> If you allow notifications on your phone, a notification token for that device, stored with your signed-in device and removed when you sign out, and your notification choices. If you use the app only on the web, we send the same notices by email. When you open a course or a session your account does not include, we may email you the page on songdance.co where it is offered, at most once per item; you can switch this off in the app’s notification settings.</p>
      <p><strong>Videos.</strong> Classes and replays play in Vimeo’s player in “do not track” mode: Vimeo sets no cookies and records no viewing session about you, and receives only what it needs to stream the video (such as your network address and device type).</p>
      <p><strong>On your device.</strong> The app keeps you signed in using your phone’s secure storage or, on the web, your browser’s local storage. The app contains no advertising, no analytics tools and no tracking, and it does not use your location.</p>
      <p><strong>About sensitive topics.</strong> What you share in the circle may say something about your emotional life or health. You decide what you share and in which space. We use it only to show it to the members of that space and to moderate it, never for anything else. By posting such content you give your explicit consent to this (Art. 9(2)(a)); you can withdraw it by deleting the post.</p>
      <p><strong>Why:</strong> to perform the contract with you and give you the courses and community you signed up for (Art. 6(1)(b)); our legitimate interest in keeping accounts secure, moderating the community, keeping a record of access changes and telling you where to find what your account does not yet include (Art. 6(1)(f)); and your consent for notifications on your device and for your WhatsApp number (Art. 6(1)(a)), which you can withdraw at any time in the app.</p>

      <h2>4. Who we share data with</h2>
      <p>We never sell personal data. We share it only with processors who help us run Songdance:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Payment providers</strong> (PayPal, credit card processing, Bancontact/iDEAL providers) — payment handling</li>
        <li><strong>Drip</strong> — email newsletter and customer emails</li>
        <li><strong>Resend</strong> — sign-in codes, account and course emails, and email notifications from the app</li>
        <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong> — hosting of the website and the Songdance app, its database and its file storage</li>
        <li><strong>Expo</strong>, with <strong>Apple Push Notification service</strong> and <strong>Google Firebase Cloud Messaging</strong> — delivering notifications to your phone, and delivering app updates</li>
        <li><strong>Vimeo</strong> — hosting and streaming course videos and replays</li>
        <li><strong>Mighty Networks</strong> — course and community hosting, until the circle has moved to the Songdance app</li>
        <li><strong>Zoom</strong> — live online sessions and recordings</li>
        <li><strong>Anthropic</strong> — AI-assisted summarization and intake preparation (see 3.6)</li>
        <li><strong>Our accountant</strong> — bookkeeping, as required by Belgian law</li>
        <li>Hosting and website infrastructure providers</li>
      </ul>
      <p>When you choose to sign in with Apple or Google, those companies handle that sign-in under their own privacy policies. There is no advertising in the app.</p>
      <p>Some of these providers are in the United States. Where data leaves the EEA, transfers are covered by the EU–US Data Privacy Framework or the European Commission’s Standard Contractual Clauses.</p>

      <h2>5. How long we keep things</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Invoices and accounting records:</strong> 7 years (Belgian legal requirement)</li>
        <li><strong>Customer account and purchase history:</strong> for as long as you have access to a program, plus 2 years</li>
        <li><strong>Newsletter data:</strong> until you unsubscribe; inactive subscribers are removed periodically</li>
        <li><strong>Session recordings:</strong> as long as any participant’s access includes them. Members see a Q&amp;A replay for a limited time after the call (currently 61 days), and some passes include lifetime access to replays</li>
        <li><strong>Intake answers:</strong> deleted within 12 months after the program ends (see 3.5)</li>
        <li><strong>Email correspondence:</strong> up to 3 years after the last exchange</li>
        <li><strong>Songdance app account:</strong> until you delete it (see section 6); your profile, devices, progress, practice availability, event sign-ups and settings go with it</li>
        <li><strong>Posts and comments:</strong> until you or a host delete them. If you delete your account, they stay visible as “Former member”, without your name or picture, unless you ask us to remove them</li>
        <li><strong>Sign-in codes and links:</strong> valid for 10 to 15 minutes, deleted within a day</li>
        <li><strong>Security counters:</strong> deleted within a day; <strong>server logs:</strong> a few days</li>
        <li><strong>Signed-in devices and notification tokens:</strong> until you sign out, and at the latest 30 days after a sign-in expires (a sign-in lasts at most 180 days)</li>
        <li><strong>Log of account and access changes:</strong> 2 years</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>6. Your rights</h2>
      <p>You have the right to access your data, correct it, have it deleted, restrict or object to its processing, take it with you (portability), and withdraw any consent you’ve given — withdrawal doesn’t affect processing that already happened.</p>
      <p>In the Songdance app you can do much of this yourself: correct your profile, remove a linked email address, sign out a device, clear your WhatsApp number, turn notifications off, delete your posts, and <strong>delete your account</strong> (Profile → Delete my account). We confirm a deletion with a code sent to your email address. Your account then closes after 14 days; if you sign in during those days, it stays open. Deleting the app account does not cancel or refund a purchase, and invoices stay for the period the law requires. You can also ask for deletion by email; more at <a href="/delete-account">songdance.co/delete-account</a>.</p>
      <p>To use any of these rights, email <a href="mailto:info@songdance.co">info@songdance.co</a>. We respond within one month. We may ask you to confirm your identity first; that’s to protect your data, not to slow you down.</p>
      <p>If you believe we’re handling your data wrongly and we can’t resolve it together, you can complain to the Belgian Data Protection Authority:</p>
      <div class="sd-legal-block">
        <p><strong>Gegevensbeschermingsautoriteit / Autorité de protection des données</strong></p>
        <p>Drukpersstraat 35, 1000 Brussels</p>
        <p><a href="https://www.dataprotectionauthority.be">www.dataprotectionauthority.be</a></p>
      </div>

      <h2>7. Children</h2>
      <p>Our programs, the Songdance app and the website are intended for adults. The app asks every member to confirm that they are 18 or older before the community opens, and it is rated for adults in the app stores. We do not knowingly collect data from anyone under 18; if you believe a minor has an account, write to us and we will close it.</p>

      <h2>8. Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>When we change this policy in any meaningful way, we’ll update the date at the top and, for significant changes, tell active customers by email. The current version always lives at songdance.co/privacy.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
